ht now if you know 50 states can have  50 different approaches to abortion  still within roe v wade that he may have  to make a ruling on  mr. chairman let me ask you a question  about about these documents you say it's  a process matter you say that the  Democrats haven't questioned these  qualifications but the documents are  about a period that Brett Kavanaugh  worked in politics when the questions in  the courts is how much politics gets  involved in laws so when Elena Kagan was  up before the committee everybody wanted  to know what she did during her time as  politics and Cavanaugh has said that  period is in many ways the most  instructive so if that period is  instructive to understanding his  jurisprudence why aren't Democrats right  to want more time to look into documents  from that period or to see documents  that haven't been turned over I think  that what Cavanaugh was saying it's very  instructive to him to to be a judge to  know what goes on in the executive  branch of government and he surely knew  what went on in the executive branch of  government because he had papers from  every cabinet member and every  intelligence agency and all that stuff  he had to decide what went to the  President or not to the president so I  interpret his station his statement is  meaning that he got very well educated  in the processes of the executive branch  so that makes him a better judge to make  decisions on on the law or the cases  that apply to the executive branch and  presidential power that's your reading  of it but you've heard me why shouldn't  Democrats get a chance to examine that  thinking based on the actual record and  not just having to guess about it yeah  because it's irrelevant to his being a  judge and not only that but remember  what Schumer and Leahy have said in the  past that the best judge of whether a  candidate should be on the Supreme Court  or not is where the cases they've  already heard in lower courts and this  person has 307 cases 10 or 11 thousand  pages that people can go by that's the  best judgment that Leahy and and Schumer  said for knowing whether somebody should  be on the Supreme Court if that's a rule  that you would use for sort of my heir  why wouldn't you use that same rule for  Cavanaugh well you got a lot of use out  of your gavel yesterday senator and  how do you intend to keep the calm today  what was your takeaway from yesterday  you know after senator McCain's funeral  there was a lot of calls for  bipartisanship  and that seemed to last a very short  time yesterday looking at what we saw in  your hearing room yesterday well I made  this statement yesterday that I think is  more true of what goes on in the United  States Senate and there's more  bipartisanship than what people see  we're very different on this judgeship  or judges generally Republican Democrats  differences but in the three-and-a-half  years that I've been chairman of the  committee every bill that has come out  of the Judiciary Committee has had  bipartisan support that speaks more  about how we work in a collegial way  than what you're seeing on television  senator in President Trump has called  jeff sessions said this guy is mentally  [ __ ] he's a dumb southerner  according to Bob Woodward's new book  would you support President Trump firing  his attorney general that's President  Trump's decision to make and I'll only  be involved in that is if he appoints a  new person all right Thank You senator  okay senator all right senator Grassley  thank you for being with us
 

